    "title": "Route 66 Capital Cruise plans to be the largest classic car parade - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By FOX23.com News Staff ,\n1 hours ago TULSA, Okla. — The official map for the Route 66 Capital Cruise was revealed on Wednesday.\nThe goal is to have more than 3,000 classic cars and form the largest classic car parade. The Capital Cruise is expected to span five and a half miles.\nCars will start at 11th Street and Yale Avenue then follow the historic Route 66 to downtown Tulsa near 10th Street and Denver Avenue.\n“When we decided that we wanted to celebrate the centennial of Route 66 as the capital of Route 66, we thought, ‘We gotta do something big. We gotta do something bold.’ So the commission and city leaders sat around the table and thought, ‘We gotta create the largest classic car parade in the world,’” said Renee McKenney, President of Tulsa Regional Tourism.\nThe event will begin on May 30, 2026, during the Route 66 Centennial celebration.\nFor more information, click here .",
